id: 12
hanzi: 点心
pinyin: diǎn xin
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: dim sum; pastry; snack; dessert; refreshment
  es: repostería; pastelitos; merienda; tentempié; dim sum

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | traditional baked, steamed, or fried cakes, dumplings, and sweet or savory snacks served between meals | pasteles, bollos o bocadillos dulces o salados que se toman como merienda o tentempié | 可口的小点心 (delicious little pastries)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 每逢周末，母亲总会亲手烘焙几样精致的点心，搭配浓郁的热红茶，让全家人享受惬意的下午茶时光。 | Měiféng zhòumò, mǔqīn zǒng huì qīnshǒu hōngbèi jǐ yàng jīngzhì de diǎnxin, dàipèi nóngyù de rè hóngchá, ràng quánjiā rén xiǎngshòu qièyì de xiàwǔchá shíguāng. | Every weekend, mother bakes delicate pastries by hand, paired with rich black tea for the family to enjoy cozy afternoon tea. | Cada fin de semana, madre hornea finos pastelitos para acompañar con té caliente, brindando una plácida merienda familiar.
  #2 | 鲁迅先生极爱甜食，下班路过北京稻香村时，总要买上几包传统的精致点心带回家中招待来客。 | Lǔ Xùn xiānsheng jí ài tiánshí, xiàbān lùguò Běijīng Dàoxiāngcūn shí, zǒng yào mǎi shàng jǐ bāo chuántǒng de jīngzhì diǎnxin dài huí jiā zhōng zhāodài láikè. | Mr. Lu Xun had a great sweet tooth; passing Daoxiangcun after work, he always bought traditional pastries to treat guests at home. | A Lu Xun le fascinaban los dulces; al pasar por la confitería Daoxiangcun compraba cajas de repostería típica para agasajar a sus visitas.

